{"id": "EUVD-2026-101244", "enisaUuid": "cc099e10-9c7f-3929-8fa1-99a1de6aff3b", "description": "NullHub through 2026.5.29 contains a missing authentication vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to access the /api/* management API because the auth_token field defaults to null and is never assigned. Attackers sending requests without Authorization or Origin headers to non-loopback listeners can control agent instances, rewrite configurations including provider credentials, and manage cron jobs and MCP servers.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T01:14:30", "baseScore": 9.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/rJrLma3izg", "https://github.com/nullclaw/nullhub/blob/v2026.5.29/src/server.zig#L546-L556", "https://github.com/nullclaw/nullhub/blob/v2026.5.29/src/api/settings.zig#L29-L54", "https://github.com/nullclaw/nullhub/blob/v2026.5.29/Dockerfile#L69-L71", "https://github.com/nullclaw/nullhub", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nullhub-through-2026.5.29-missing-authentication-for-api-management-api"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110616", "GHSA-jrqq-fxff-7f78"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.81, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "bcb2fb3b-997d-3dc6-9c32-f802ec8a5aab", "product": {"name": "NullHub", "vendor": {"name": "nullclaw"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642026.5.29"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c1d6ee51-525f-3649-8147-6525fbedc121", "vendor": {"name": "nullclaw"}}], "isExploited": false}